part.text:
Confirmed: option click auto-advances (and auto-submits on last). My #next clicks each double-advanced — that's why it errored on the last (after 18 option clicks it was already at result; the 18th #next was null). Interesting: it still produced a full answer set (answers[idx] gets overwritten by double advances — some questions got answers via next-button requiring prior selection... whatever, the flow completed with all answers defined because option clicks happened 18 times with index bouncing... Actually the double-advance pattern: click option[0] → answers[0]=0, index→1, re-render; then my #next click → answers[1] undefined → returns without advancing (guard: `if (state.answers[state.index] === undefined) return;`). So no double advance. Then next iteration i=1 clicks .option[1] on Q2 → answers[1]=1... So each loop iteration answered exactly one question via option click; #next was a no-op guard... until the last question: option click → renderResult() → #next gone → my redundant click threw. 

So answers were all set properly. The fix: remove the #next click entirely, and wait between questions for the DOM to be ready. Rewrite that loop:

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 18; i += 1) {
  for (let t = 0; t < 20; t += 1) {
    if (await evaluate(`document.querySelectorAll('.option').length > 0`)) break;
    await sleep(200);
  }
  await evaluate(`document.querySelectorAll('.option')[${i % 3}].click()`);
  await sleep(300);
}
```
Then the result-wait loop as before. Also note the run consumed nothing extra — code stays valid (re-entry with secret). But localStorage in the Chrome profile has the license; my script re-runs redeem with code only → already activated, secret mismatch (no secret sent) → 403 already_bound! For re-runs, first check localStorage or use verify with stored secret. Simplest: on rerun, evaluate localStorage.getItem first; if present, reuse; else redeem. Update script accordingly.

Also the current profile already has license + finished state; since script re-navigates and answers again, fine.

