Now validator in creators.mjs — extend FORMATS and add per-format branches:
- visual: q 6–10, results 4–6, options 2–4, each option requires `swatch` (#hex)
- scenario: q 8–12, results 5–7, options 2–4, optional `scene` per question (≤14 chars)
- axis4: axes 2–4, questions 6–16 (每个轴至少 2 题), options exactly 2, scores {axis: ±1}, results = 2^axes with combo arrays, unique coverage
- pair: archetype fence but questions even count (8–16), pair flag
- draw: no questions, results 3–12, no scores; reading required (already in field checks)

Let me edit FORMATS + add branches. Current FORMATS block and validation sections need care:

```js
const FORMATS = {
  archetype: { questionMin: 12, questionMax: 16, resultMin: 6, resultMax: 8, options: [3, 3] },
  index: {...},
  choice2: {...},
  visual: { questionMin: 6, questionMax: 10, resultMin: 4, resultMax: 6, options: [2, 4] },
  scenario: { questionMin: 8, questionMax: 12, resultMin: 5, resultMax: 7, options: [2, 4] },
  axis4: special (axes-driven),
  pair: { questionMin: 8, questionMax: 16, resultMin: 4, resultMax: 8, options: [2, 4] },
  draw: { questionMin: 0, questionMax: 0, resultMin: 3, resultMax: 12 },
};
```

axis4 handled specially: fence from axes count. In validateCreatorContent:
```js
if (format === "axis4") {
  axes = Array.isArray(input?.axes) ? input.axes.filter(a => /^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,15}$/.test(a)) : [];
  if (axes.length < 2 || axes.length > 4) errors.push("axis4 需要声明 2–4 个轴（axes 数组）");
  fence = { questionMin: axes.length * 2, questionMax: 16, resultMin: 2 ** axes.length, resultMax: 2 ** axes.length, options: [2, 2] };
}
```
Careful: fence used before questions validated. For axis4 with invalid axes → 2**0=1 resultMin... if axes invalid, errors already pushed; guard resultMin max(2,...).

Questions loop: options count fence; scores checks: for axis4, each option scores exactly {axisId: ±1} where q.axis declared:
```js
if (format === "axis4") {
  if (!q.axis || !axes.includes(q.axis)) errors.push(`第 ${i+1} 题缺少合法的 axis 标注`);
  else if (entries.length !== 1 || entries[0][0] !== q.axis || ![1,-1].includes(entries[0][1])) errors.push(...只能给本题轴 ±1...);
}
```
Bounds: for axis4, normalization per result not needed; selectWinner uses sign only. bounds computed anyway harmless (ids loop) — for axis4 options scores reference axis ids not result ids → "给未声明的结果计分" check must skip axis ids for axis4: entries keys are axis ids, not result ids → current check `if (!ids.has(rid)) errors...` would false-error. Guard: for axis4, valid score keys = axes; skip result-id check.

Combo coverage check (axis4): results need combo arrays covering all 2^n sign vectors exactly once:
```js
const seen = new Set();
for (const r of results) {
  const combo = r.combo;
  valid = Array.isArray(combo) && combo.length === axes.length && combo.every(v => v === 1 || v === -1);
  key = combo.join(",");
  if seen → dup error; seen.add
}
if (seen.size !== 2**axes.length) errors.push(`axis4 结果必须覆盖全部 ${2**axes.length} 种轴组合（缺 X 种）`)
```

pair: theme.pair = true; questions length must be even.
draw: questions must be empty; options checks skipped; results field checks same; no scores anywhere; no bounds needed (skip reachability); theme without scoring? selectWinner not called. Server picks seeded. Set scoring: null.

Reachability section: skip for draw and axis4 (axis4 has its own combo coverage = full determinism); pair uses archetype-style lean-run (same engine). index has own. visual/scenario/choice2/archetype → existing loop.

Dominance: for axis4 with all-16-combos covered and 3 questions per axis: random answers → each axis sum random walk of 3 steps of ±1 → sign distribution roughly balanced; combos each ~1/16 ≈ 18 wins/300 ✓ no dominance issue. But careful: if questions per axis odd (3), sum ∈ {-3,-1,1,3}, sign never 0 → fine. Even questions per axis (e.g., 2): sum ∈ {-2,0,2} → 0 → -1 → slight bias; acceptable.

structure of theme: include axes for axis4, pair flag for pair.

theme.build: `if (format === "axis4") { theme.axes = axes; }` `if (format === "pair") theme.pair = true;` draw: no scoring key.

Also the scoredIds/bounds loop: for axis4 ids are result slugs but options don't score them → values all 0 → bounds zeros; harmless since selectWinner doesn't use bounds for axis4. For draw: no questions → loop over questions empty → bounds zeros; skip anyway. Simplify: compute bounds only for formats that use them (index axis; archetype-family reachability needs bounds for selectWinner) — visual/scenario/choice2/archetype/pair use bounds; index uses; axis4/draw skip.

